{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20","id":1300819,"title":"Circumventing Metis deformities W20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-29T06:49:16-07:00","id":1300819,"title":"Circumventing Metis deformities W20","content":"Pretty much what it says on the title, is there any merit, gift or mage/vampire power that can eliminate or mitigate the deformities that Metis face?<br /> <br /> My current idea is Vicissitude 2 (Fleshcraft) and the deformities: <b>Hip Dysplasia, Horns, Hunchback, Monstrous, Third Eye, </b>and <b>Tough Hide</b>. I am not sure if the Metis would just heal the modification (and if it will keep at least the Tough Hide extra soak die).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-29-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:28:45-07:00","id":1300830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20#post1300819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what it says on the title, is there any merit, gift or mage/vampire power that can eliminate or mitigate the deformities that Metis face?<br /> <br /> My current idea is Vicissitude 2 (Fleshcraft) and the deformities: <b>Hip Dysplasia, Horns, Hunchback, Monstrous, Third Eye, </b>and <b>Tough Hide</b>. I am not sure if the Metis would just heal the modification (and if it will keep at least the Tough Hide extra soak die).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup he would heal it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T10:27:44-07:00","id":1300875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20#post1300819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what it says on the title, is there any merit, gift or mage/vampire power that can eliminate or mitigate the deformities that Metis face?<br /> <br /> My current idea is Vicissitude 2 (Fleshcraft) and the deformities: <b>Hip Dysplasia, Horns, Hunchback, Monstrous, Third Eye, </b>and <b>Tough Hide</b>. I am not sure if the Metis would just heal the modification (and if it will keep at least the Tough Hide extra soak die).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember Vicissitude is healed as agg damage (ST handbook revised.) Other than that, metis deformities are mystical in nature. I think I've seen only ONE time that a metis deformity was healed, in Glass Walkers revised and that metis then gained a new deformity to jam technology.<br /> <br /> If your third eye gets plucked out, it might cause re-ocurring headaches. If your horns are cut off, they might either regrow back even worse or result in mangy flesh near the cut off spot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T10:35:12-07:00","id":1300878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20#post1300819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what it says on the title, is there any merit, gift or mage/vampire power that can eliminate or mitigate the deformities that Metis face?<br /> <br /> My current idea is Vicissitude 2 (Fleshcraft) and the deformities: <b>Hip Dysplasia, Horns, Hunchback, Monstrous, Third Eye, </b>and <b>Tough Hide</b>. I am not sure if the Metis would just heal the modification (and if it will keep at least the Tough Hide extra soak die).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Naming 5 should do it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T13:40:28-07:00","id":1300935,"title":"","content":"Another mitigation strategy not for deformities but for a general weakness, the Silver Tolerance merit states: &quot;You may soak silver damage in any form at difficulty 8&quot;<br /> <br /> Will this override Metis' inability to soak silver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-29-2019, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T05:41:26-07:00","id":1301063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1300935#post1300935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another mitigation strategy not for deformities but for a general weakness, the Silver Tolerance merit states: &quot;You may soak silver damage in any form at difficulty 8&quot;<br /> <br /> Will this override Metis' inability to soak silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T06:59:06-07:00","id":1301073,"title":"","content":"If you don't want that many deformities, why did your character have so many? You are really only required maybe two tops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T07:24:13-07:00","id":1301075,"title":"","content":"There are plenty of &quot;nondeforminty&quot; Deformity options in there if you just want gifts... like &quot;Unnatural hair color&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T08:18:36-07:00","id":1301079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301075#post1301075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of &quot;nondeforminty&quot; Deformity options in there if you just want gifts... like &quot;Unnatural hair color&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastial reflection, snake tongue, foul odor. There are many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T11:55:20-07:00","id":1301113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301073#post1301073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want that many deformities, why did your character have so many? You are really only required maybe two tops.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it has more than one, I was looking for ways to mitigate the worst ones. Basically, I am considering a mixed game, in which some idiots are trying to create an army of Metis, eliminating drawbacks, with the aim of creating an artificial Perfect Metis.<br /> <br /> Also, a bit of metagaming with Metis deformities, to optimize for combat. The best ones (FOR COMBAT) would be <b>Hirsute</b>, and <b>Tough Hide</b>. The latter more so than the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T12:00:35-07:00","id":1301114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301075#post1301075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of &quot;nondeforminty&quot; Deformity options in there if you just want gifts... like &quot;Unnatural hair color&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the option of using freebies to raise Willpower to the maximum possible, and getting <b>Fits of Madness</b>, or <b>Seizures</b>. With a difficulty of 8, 10 dice give you on average slightly more than 3 successes. And of course, you have 10 willpower points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T12:30:17-07:00","id":1301116,"title":"","content":"Why you don't just ban stuff and play a normal nice story ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T12:57:14-07:00","id":1301123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301113#post1301113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said it has more than one, I was looking for ways to mitigate the worst ones. Basically, I am considering a mixed game, in which some idiots are trying to create an army of Metis, eliminating drawbacks, with the aim of creating an artificial Perfect Metis.<br /> <br /> Also, a bit of metagaming with Metis deformities, to optimize for combat. The best ones (FOR COMBAT) would be <b>Hirsute</b>, and <b>Tough Hide</b>. The latter more so than the former.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bring the Apis back from the Dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:19:13-07:00","id":1301388,"title":"","content":"Mmmmm, healing and mitigating (and concealing through the both) Metis deformities... hard to do and if successful bye bye renown!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:02:45-07:00","id":1301398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301388#post1301388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmm, healing and mitigating (and concealing through the both) Metis deformities... hard to do and if successful bye bye renown!</div> </div> </div> </div>But it wont be hiding if you can actually heal them. The Silver Tolerance merit is an ability all Garou COULD possess, why that merit would cost the Metis renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:48:50-07:00","id":1301412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301113#post1301113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said it has more than one, I was looking for ways to mitigate the worst ones. Basically, I am considering a mixed game, in which some idiots are trying to create an army of Metis, eliminating drawbacks, with the aim of creating an artificial Perfect Metis.<br /> <br /> Also, a bit of metagaming with Metis deformities, to optimize for combat. The best ones (FOR COMBAT) would be <b>Hirsute</b>, and <b>Tough Hide</b>. The latter more so than the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating an army of metis is more costly than an army of lupus. For one, you need like 50 female garou, hope they don't DIE during childbirth or become infertile. Then you have to hope the deformities of the metis don't make them useless. Then you better hope any of the female garou don't try to tear the baby off/kill themselves during the 9 month long pregnancy. Then you have 10 years to raise the ragy baby before they can be used in an army.<br /> <br /> There is a reason BSDs don't solely rely on their metis numbers.<br /> <br /> A faster and a more reliable way to get garou shock troops would be to get some lupus garou, some wolf kinfolk and just breed them until garou cubs pop out. They take 2 years to mature, the pregnancy lasts 2 months and they can still breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:44:43-07:00","id":1301461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301398#post1301398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it wont be hiding if you can actually heal them. The Silver Tolerance merit is an ability all Garou COULD possess, why that merit would cost the Metis renown?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not being able to soak Silver isn't a Metis deformity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:55:17-07:00","id":1301546,"title":"","content":"It's only useful for one specific deformity, but having <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Piggi-Billa\" target=\"_blank\">Piggi-Billa the Echidna</a> as your totem lets you cure Weak Claws in exchange for a permanent gnosis point. Plus he doesn't have a ban for metis characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:15:05-07:00","id":1301697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301461#post1301461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not being able to soak Silver isn't a Metis deformity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was a deformity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1300935#post1300935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another mitigation strategy <b>not for deformities but for a general weakness</b>, the Silver Tolerance merit states: &quot;You may soak silver damage in any form at difficulty 8&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe mitigating is not the way, but accumulating redundant deformities: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Select the Metis deformity: <b>Tough Hide</b>.</li> <li>Pick the Flaw: <b>Double Jeopardy</b>, and as your second deformity, pick <b>Hirsute </b>(for the extra soak in some forms) or <b>Monstruous </b>(to put in zero a trait you could not raise from 1).</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> Would this be viable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-07-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:36:49-07:00","id":1301763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301697#post1301697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this be viable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I doubt that any GM worth his salt will ever approve this kind of thing. The point of having flaws is to RP them and the extra points you get are for balancing, but Monstrous is not a flaw if you have Tough Hide and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Metis deformities are also an (allegied) mark from Gaia and you're not supposed to conceal them, let alone remove. Probably some master mage is able to alter your life/spirit pattern (or mind/spirit in case of derangements - i'm including spirit because of the unique half-spirit nature of the Garou) and mend every deformity but that's a serious defiance of Gaia IMHO. If I were the storyteller I could even remove enough permanent honor to drop you a rank and forbid you to ever gain more until you're restored. That Metis might even be cast out and become a Ronin.<br /> <br /> But that might be worth anyway for a character that lived her past twenty years struggling with a split personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25122-theroseblack","name":"TheRoseBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:30:01-07:00","id":1303558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheRoseBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301763#post1301763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I doubt that any GM worth his salt will ever approve this kind of thing. The point of having flaws is to RP them and the extra points you get are for balancing, but Monstrous is not a flaw if you have Tough Hide and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Metis deformities are also an (allegied) mark from Gaia and you're not supposed to conceal them, let alone remove. Probably some master mage is able to alter your life/spirit pattern (or mind/spirit in case of derangements - I'm including spirit because of the unique half-spirit nature of the Garou) and mend every deformity but that's a serious defiance of Gaia IMHO. If I were the storyteller I could even remove enough permanent honor to drop you a rank and forbid you to ever gain more until you're restored. That Metis might even be cast out and become a Ronin.<br /> <br /> But that might be worth anyway for a character that lived her past twenty years struggling with a split personality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, after posting this question, I participated in a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">V20 discussion about Vampires vs Werewolves</a>. I ended up making a character to show what happens if you optimize for combat using a W20 starting build with a Totem (<i>Hummingbird</i>) and a a Sept Totem (<i>Wolverine</i>) from W20 Rage Across the World, p.29:<br /> <br /> <b>Ugly McAngry</b><br /> Breed: Metis<br /> Auspice: Ahroun<br /> Tribe: Children of Gaia<br /> Nature: Competitor<br /> Demeanor: Big Bad Wolf<br /> Rank: 1<br /> Physical: Strength 4 (6/8/7/5) (Claws), Dexterity 7 (7/8/9/9) (Dodging), Stamina 2 (4/5/5/4)<br /> Social: Charisma 4 (Gnosis), Manipulation 1 (0/0/0/0), Appearance 0 (0/0/0/0)<br /> Mental: Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 5 ((Combat Reflexes))<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 5 (Claws), Intimidation 1, Primal-Urge 3<br /> Skills: Etiquette 1, Stealth 3, Survival 1<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Enigmas 3, Investigation 1, Law 1, Medicine 1, Occult 1, Rituals 1<br /> Backgrounds: Fetish 4 (Soul of Lightning), Totem 1 (Hummingbird)<br /> Rage: 6<br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Glory: 2<br /> Honor: 1<br /> Wisdom: 0<br /> Metis deformity: Eyes of Darkness, Tough Hide<br /> Gifts: (1) Razor Claws, Resist Pain, Sense Wyrm; (2) Spirit of the Fray<br /> Rites: None<br /> Merits: Berserker, Mars Midsky, Self-Confident<br /> Flaws: Double Jeopardy, Impatient, Monstrous<br /> <br /> <br /> All freebies spent on Berserker, Brawl, Mars Midsky, Self-Confident, and Willpower; this fellow can:<ul><li>Win Initiative most of the time. <i>Max Dexterity + Max Wits + Spirit of the Fray</i></li> <li>Attack several times per turn. <i>Max Rage + Wolverine</i></li> <li>Hit enemies consistently. <i>Max Dexterity + Max Brawl + Specialty</i></li> <li>Do large amounts of damage. <i>High Strength + Claws + Razor Claws + </i><i>Soul of Lightning</i><i> + </i><i>Mars Midsky + Specialty + Attack roll bonus</i></li> <li>Get lots of automatic successes<i>. Max Willpower + Self-Confident</i></li> <li>Ignore most forms of mind control<i>. Max Willpower</i></li> <li>Recover Willpower after each fight<i>. </i><i>Competitor</i></li> <li>Get 2 extra Dexterity dots and the gift: Spirit of the Fray. <i>Hummingbird</i></li> <li>Get 1 extra Stamina dot and a Rage dot that can never be lost. <i>Wolverine</i></li> <li>Stun enemies when doing at least 4 points of damage (after soak).<i> Soul of Lightning</i></li> <li>Avoid ambushes by Wyrm tainted creatures. <i>Primal-Urge + Sense Wyrm</i></li> <li>Regenerate in every form. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Assume Crinos form instantly. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Enter a Berserk Frenzy at will, ignoring wound penalties and gaining +2 soak and +1 Strength die. <i>Berserker + Mars Midsky</i>\u200b\u200b</li> <li>Soak a regular amount of damage. <i>Low Stamina + Tough Hide + Mars Midsky</i>\u200b</li> <li>Ignore all wound penalties for a scene. <i>Resist Pain</i></li> <li>See perfectly in darkness<i>. Eyes of Darkness</i></li> <li>Cheap access to some of the best gifts: (1) Falling Touch, Jam Weapon, Mother\u2019s Touch, Razor Claws, Resist Pain, Sense Wyrm; (2) Burrow, Form Mastery, Luna\u2019s Armor, Grandmother\u2019s Touch, Spirit of the Fray, True Fear; (3) Calm the Savage Beast, Chameleon, Combat Healing, Dazzle, Mental Speech, Rage of the Underdog, Shell, Silver Claws, The Cleaving Hoof; (4) Full Moon's Light, Gift of the Porcupine, Lash of Rage, Rattler's Bite, Stoking Fury\u2019s Furnace, Strike the Air, Tenacious Fury; (5) Halo of the Sun, Kiss of Helios, Protean Form, Strength of Will, Totem Gift; (6) Unstoppable Warrior. <i>Metis + Ahroun + Children of Gaia</i></li> <li>Buy future traits as cheaply as possible.</li> </ul>And now I just wonder if is there any way to mitigate whatever weaknesses the character might have, FROM CHARACTER CREATION.<b> <u>I am aware that CWOD is not D&amp;D.</u></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-07-2026, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:30:31-08:00","id":1345959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20#post1300819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what it says on the title, is there any merit, gift or mage/vampire power that can eliminate or mitigate the deformities that Metis face?<br /> <br /> My current idea is Vicissitude 2 (Fleshcraft) and the deformities: <b>Hip Dysplasia, Horns, Hunchback, Monstrous, Third Eye, </b>and <b>Tough Hide</b>. I am not sure if the Metis would just heal the modification (and if it will keep at least the Tough Hide extra soak die).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there's a level 10 discipline, ir level 6 ritual called &quot; Storyteller Says So&quot; thar fixes that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:20:57-08:00","id":1345975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1345959#post1345959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah there's a level 10 discipline, ir level 6 ritual called &quot; Storyteller Says So&quot; thar fixes that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it in Necromancy, by any chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:43:22-08:00","id":1345990,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> that is a REALLY powerful character!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:51:49-08:00","id":1346011,"title":"","content":"It's a very min-maxed character that's brutal in close combat.<br /> <br /> Ways to ruin their day:<br /> <br /> 1) Multiple enemies (Rage burns quick even with Primal Anger which just makes you easier to beat).<br /> <br /> 2) Enemies at range (so they don't get murdered up close, and forces spending Rage to close).<br /> <br /> 3) Has Rage &gt; Gnosis and 10 dice on Frenzy checks. Wait for a full moon, piss them off and watch them murder their pack and/or allies (if in the Umbra and his Totem is around for a personal Totem build.... their Totem spirit is going to be super pissed off too), since 6+ successes means they can't spend WP to avoid the Frenzy and goes full Thrall.<br /> <br /> 4) Force them into any sort of social or mental challenges and watch them fail, get angry, Frenzy, and get put down by thei Sept. He might look really scary to go after with a stare down contest, but odds are they'll Frenzy and lose. They also automatically fail game-craft challenges.<br /> <br /> 5) They can't go out in public with Rage like that, so any confrontation around normal people is going to add lots of cannon fodder to the mix to drain that WP and Rage.<br /> <br /> 6) Lots of mind whammy powers don't have Willpower as a difficulty and thus can mess this build up hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:03:48-08:00","id":1346087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1301113#post1301113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said it has more than one, I was looking for ways to mitigate the worst ones. Basically, I am considering a mixed game, in which some idiots are trying to create an army of Metis, eliminating drawbacks, with the aim of creating an artificial Perfect Metis.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those idiots WILL anger the spirits... I hope they're prepared for some serious backlash<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T02:24:33-08:00","id":1346107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346087#post1346087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those idiots WILL anger the spirits... I hope they're prepared for some serious backlash</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet in Changing Ways, this was treated as an acceptable practice by some septs.<br /> <br /> ....yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:40:08-08:00","id":1346136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1345990#post1345990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> that is a REALLY powerful character!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just in close quarters combat. It is literally impossible to optimize an starting character against everything. The advantage of Werewolves is that a lot of their powers apply to the whole pack, synergy covering a lot of weak points.<br /> <br /> <br /> To optimize an starting character to beat all comers, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters\">I would have gone with a </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters\">Mage</a>, because prepared mages are pretty close to invincible. That being said <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I did ask for ways to mitigate weaknesses and I will try to tackle those you mentioned, plus I have edited the original post to make it less imbalanced but still brutal in close combat:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a very min-maxed character that's brutal in close combat.<br /> <br /> Ways to ruin their day:<br /> <br /> 1) Multiple enemies (Rage burns quick even with Primal Anger which just makes you easier to beat).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but a Pack should give you multiple allies. There is no starting build that is able to defeat a sufficiently large number of enemies, at most withdraw, and in that spirit, I add <i>Mirrorshades</i> to the build while removing <i>Primal Anger</i>. And since we are assuming a Pack, I will only use a single dot of Totem for its benefits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Enemies at range (so they don't get murdered up close, and forces spending Rage to close).</div> </div> </div> </div>Changed the totem to Hummingbird, for the <i>Spirit of the Fray</i> and go first, and switched <i>Resist Pain</i> for <i>Jam Weapon</i>, so weapon-wielding enemies are forced into hand to hand combat. Added <i>Acute Sense 3 (Hearing, Sight, Smell)</i> and <i>Sense Wyrm </i>to detect some enemies before they appear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Has Rage &gt; Gnosis and 10 dice on Frenzy checks. Wait for a full moon, piss them off and watch them murder their pack and/or allies (if in the Umbra and his Totem is around for a personal Totem build.... their Totem spirit is going to be super pissed off too), since 6+ successes means they can't spend WP to avoid the Frenzy and goes full Thrall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping Rage at 5 plus using the <i>Foul Temper</i> flaw (to diminish the rage build-up) helps with this, and leaves enough freebies to tackle other problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Force them into any sort of social or mental challenges and watch them fail, get angry, Frenzy, and get put down by thei Sept. He might look really scary to go after with a stare down contest, but odds are they'll Frenzy and lose. They also automatically fail game-craft challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character is not going to fail ALL mental or social challenges, max Wits and high Charisma still provide good traits for Talent rolls, but I will change the social stats; let's redistribute the Skills and Knowledges dots, remove <i>Harano Prone</i>, and add the merits <i>Concentration </i>to reduce penalties, <i>Lu<i>cky </i></i>to defend against failures and <i>Self-Confident</i>, to get more bang-per-buck from spending Willpower dots specially in challenging situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) They can't go out in public with Rage like that, so any confrontation around normal people is going to add lots of cannon fodder to the mix to drain that WP and Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>See points 3 and 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1300819-circumventing-metis-deformities-w20?p=1346011#post1346011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Lots of mind whammy powers don't have Willpower as a difficulty and thus can mess this build up hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>With <i>Lu</i><i><i>cky </i></i>and <i>Self-Confident</i>, more chances to survive any mind power, either a flat reroll or spending Willpower to succeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming the Pack helps carry the cost of the Totem (<i>Hummingbird</i>) and that a Sept Totem (<i>Polar Bear</i>) is used:<br /> <br /> <br /> Breed: Metis<br /> Auspice: Ahroun<br /> Tribe: Children of Gaia<br /> Nature: Competitor<br /> Demeanor: Soldier<br /> Rank: 1<br /> Physical: Strength 5 (7/9/8/6) (Claws), Dexterity 7 (7/8/9/9) (Dodging), Stamina 2 (4/5/5/4)<br /> Social: Charisma 4 (Imposing), Manipulation 1 (0/0/0/0), Appearance 1 (0/0/1/1)<br /> Mental: Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Intimidation 1, Primal-Urge 3<br /> Skills: Etiquette 1, Stealth 3, Survival 1<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Enigmas 3, Investigation 1, Law 1, Medicine 1, Occult 1, Rituals 1<br /> Backgrounds: Ancestors 5, Totem 1 (Hummingbird)<br /> Rage: 5<br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Glory: 2<br /> Honor: 1<br /> Wisdom: 0<br /> Metis deformity: Eyes of Darkness, Tough Hide<br /> Gifts: (1) Jam Weapon, Razor Claws, Sense Wyrm; (2) Spirit of the Fray<br /> Rites: None<br /> Merits: Acute Sense 3 (Hearing, Sight, Smell), Ancestor Ally, Concentration, Lucky, Self-Confident, Supporter<br /> Flaws: Double Jeopardy, Foul Temper, Impatient, Overconfident<br /> <br /> <br /> All freebies spent on Acute Sense, Ancestor Ally, Concentration, Lucky, Self-Confident, Supporter, and Willpower; to be able of:<ul><li>Win Initiative most of the time. <i>Max Dexterity + Max Wits + Spirit of the Fray</i></li> <li>Attack up to three times per turn. <i>Rage 5</i></li> <li>Force weapon using enemies to enter hand-to-hand combat. <i>Jam Weapon</i></li> <li>Hit enemies consistently. <i>Max Dexterity + High Brawl + Specialty</i></li> <li>Do large amounts of damage. <i>Max Strength + Claws + Razor Claws + Specialty + Attack roll bonus</i></li> <li>Get lots of automatic successes<i>. Max Willpower + Self-Confident</i></li> <li>Able to ignore most forms of mind control<i>. Max Willpower + Lucky + Self-Confident</i></li> <li>Recover Willpower after each fight<i>. </i><i>Competitor</i></li> <li>Get 2 extra Dexterity dots and the gift: Spirit of the Fray. <i>Hummingbird</i></li> <li>Get 1 extra Stamina and Strength dot, once per day access to the gift: Mother\u2019s Touch, regrow limbs with a Willpower point, and the pack gets 2 extra dots of Brawl and Medicine. <i>Polar Bear</i></li> <li>Avoid ambushes by most creatures, specially Wyrm tainted. <i>Acute Sense (Hearing, Sight, Smell) + Sense Wyrm + Primal-Urge</i></li> <li>Extra dice when needed. <i>Ancestors + Ancestor Ally</i></li> <li>Reroll failed rolls. <i>Lucky</i></li> <li>-2 to all Social rolls and +1 die to all group efforts. <i>Supporter</i></li> <li>Ignore circumstantial penalties to dice pools or difficulty ratings. <i>Concentration</i></li> <li>Regenerate in every form. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Assume Crinos form instantly. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Soak some damage. <i>Low Stamina + Tough Hide</i></li> <li>See perfectly in darkness<i>. Eyes of Darkness</i></li> <li>Cheap access to some of the best combat gifts: (1) Jam Weapon, Mother\u2019s Touch, Primal Anger, Razor Claws, Resist Pain, Rhythm of War, Sense Wyrm; (2) Burrow, Calm, Luna\u2019s Armor, Grandmother\u2019s Touch, Spirit of the Fray, Unicorn\u2019s Arsenal; (3) Combat Healing, Dazzle, Rage of the Underdog, Silver Claws, The Cleaving Hoof, Wind Claws; (4) Stoking Fury\u2019s Furnace, Tenacious Fury; (5) Halo of the Sun, Kiss of Helios; (6) Unstoppable Warrior. <i>Metis + Ahroun + Children of Gaia</i></li> <li>Buy future traits as cheap as possible.</li> </ul>Still a combat monster but more balanced, covering nearly all weaknesses described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-19-2026, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}